{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumDilogarithm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumDilogarithm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.realQSaddle_phi_q_ne_phi_q_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.realQSaddle_phi_q_ne_phi_q_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L218-L227","doc":"**Conditional corollary.** Under the saddle conjecture, the real-`q` saddle\nof the compact-q-dilog face disagrees with `phi_q` itself at zero amplitude (the\nRogers face is `0` there, the Faddeev face is `1`): the saddle genuinely\nmoves `phi_q` off its own value, witnessing that the real-`q` continuation is\nthe bounded Rogers form, not the Faddeev product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.realQSaddle_phi_q_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.realQSaddle_phi_q_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L207-L216","doc":"**Conditional corollary (non-vacuous).** Under the saddle conjecture, the\nreal-`q` saddle of the Faddeev face vanishes at zero amplitude — derived by\nrewriting along the conjecture and then applying the *proven*\n`towerTerm_at_zero`. Composes the hypothesis with an established lemma; does\nnot assume the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle.saddle_phi_q_eq_towerTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle.saddle_phi_q_eq_towerTerm","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L205-L205","doc":"CONJECTURE: the real-`q` saddle of the Faddeev face is the Rogers\nproduction tower term. Open for `𝓑₃` (AJ-saddle identification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle.realQSaddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle.realQSaddle","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L202-L202","doc":"the real-`q` archimedean saddle, acting on a dilogarithm face. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle.mk","kind":"ctor","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L200-L200","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZHabiroRogersSaddle","kind":"class","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L195-L205","doc":"**Conjecture (z-Habiro Rogers saddle identity).** There is a real-`q`\narchimedean saddle map `realQSaddle` under which the compact-q-dilog face `phi_q`\nbecomes the bounded Rogers production tower term `towerTerm = -li2_q(-|·|)`.\nThe `saddle_phi_q_eq_towerTerm` field is the conjectural input — open for\n`𝓑₃`; every result below is conditional on this class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumDilogarithm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumDilogarithm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L169-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumDilogarithm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuantumDilogarithm","kind":"structure","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L167-L169","doc":"Quantum-dilogarithm disambiguation (placeholder marker for content block ref resolution) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-dilogarithm-disambiguation","label":"def:quantum-dilogarithm-disambiguation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quantum-dilogarithm-disambiguation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ne_phi_q_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ne_phi_q_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L158-L164","doc":"Any class instance using the corrected form **disagrees** with\n`phi_q` at z = 0 (since Φ_q(q, 0) = 1 ≠ 0 = towerTerm(q, 0)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.archimedeanSpec_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.archimedeanSpec_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L151-L156","doc":"Any class instance using the corrected form vanishes at zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower.uses_li2q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower.uses_li2q","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L149-L149","doc":"The instance uses the corrected `-Li_2^q(-|V|)` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower.archimedeanSpec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower.archimedeanSpec","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L147-L147","doc":"The archimedean specialisation function used in this instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower.mk","kind":"ctor","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasCorrectedMassEndomorphismTower","kind":"class","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L140-L149","doc":"**Anti-regression discipline.** Any consumer of the mass-\nendomorphism tower that takes `f` as the archimedean\nspecialisation function should assert\n`f = towerTerm`, not `f = phi_q`. The latter is the historical\npathological form preserved only as a diagnostic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_at_zero_ne_towerTerm_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_at_zero_ne_towerTerm_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L133-L138","doc":"At zero amplitude the historical Φ_q form is 1, NOT 0. This\nis the elementary witness that the historical identity fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.towerTerm_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.towerTerm_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L127-L131","doc":"At zero amplitude the corrected tower term vanishes:\n`towerTerm q 0 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.towerTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.towerTerm","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L116-L125","doc":"**Canonical tower form (corrected).** The mass-endomorphism\ntower uses `-Li_2^q(-|V|)` on per-generator amplitudes, NOT\n`Φ_q(|V|)`. The corrected per-generator term is:\n\n  towerTerm q V = -li2_q q (-|V|)\n\nEmpirically bounded; Markov-invariant via the Plancherel-series\nfactoring of each `z^n` summand through tr_M(σ_i^n) (see\n`brane_tower_plancherel_scaffold.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_ne_li2_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_ne_li2_q","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L103-L114","doc":"The two functions are **NOT** equal under the historical\nidentity claim `Φ_q(z) = -Li_2^q(-z)`. The proof exhibits a\ncounter-example at `z = 0`, where Φ_q is the empty product\n`1` and -Li_2^q(-0) is the empty sum `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.li2_q_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.li2_q_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L96-L101","doc":"Empty-sum convention: Li_2^q(q, 0) = 0 for every q. **Theorem**\n(was previously an axiom). Discharged by `def li2_q` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.li2_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.li2_q","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L89-L94","doc":"Symmetric q-dilogarithm encoded as the empty-sum baseline `0`\nplus a `z`-multiplied residual factor. The `li2_q_residual` axiom\nabstracts everything beyond the empty-sum term (`li2_q_residual q 0`\nis the linear-in-`z` coefficient; the residual for `z ≠ 0` carries\nall higher-order behaviour). Parallel construction to `phi_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.li2_q_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.li2_q_residual","kind":"opaque","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L72-L87","doc":"The **symmetric q-dilogarithm** evaluated at `z`. Defined as\n\n  Li_2^q(z) = Σ_{n ≥ 1} z^n / (n · [n]_q)\n\nwhere `[n]_q = (q^n − q^{-n}) / (q − q^{-1})` is the q-bracket.\n\nEquivalently (Kashaev integration limit identity):\n\n  −Li_2^q(−z) = ∫_0^z (ln_q(1+t) / t) dt.\n\nBounded in [0.1, 0.82] for z ∈ (0, 1) at q_0 — this is the\ncorrect archimedean specialisation of `Vol_q^(S)` in the\nmass-endomorphism tower. The series has empty first term at\nz = 0, giving Li_2^q(q, 0) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L65-L70","doc":"Empty-product convention: Φ_q(q, 0) = 1 for every q. **Theorem**\n(was previously an axiom). Discharged by `def phi_q` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L54-L63","doc":"Quantum dilogarithm encoded as the empty-product baseline `1`\nplus a `z`-multiplied residual factor. The `phi_q_residual`\naxiom abstracts everything beyond the empty-product term (so\n`phi_q_residual q 0` is the linear-in-`z` coefficient, with\n`phi_q_residual q z` for `z ≠ 0` carrying all higher-order\nbehaviour). This is a strict improvement over a free\n`phi_q_at_zero` axiom: the empty-product convention is now a\n*theorem* — only Φ_q's variation away from `z = 0` stays\nopaque. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.phi_q_residual","kind":"opaque","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuantumDilogarithm.lean#L36-L52","doc":"The **quantum dilogarithm product** at substrate `q` and\nargument `z`. Defined formally as the infinite product\n\n  Φ_q(z) = ∏_{k=1}^∞ (1 - q^{-k} z)^{-1}.\n\nAt z = 0 the product is empty, giving Φ_q(q, 0) = 1.\nUnbounded near |z| = 1 (concretely, Φ_q(0.989) ≈ 6.7 × 10^5 at\nq_0 ≈ 1.110). Used in `mass_endomorphism.py` and\n`brane_tower_isospin_diagnosis.py` (the latter as a *diagnostic*\nthat exposes the −737 MeV mirror-nucleus pathology when the\narchimedean specialisation is taken to be Φ_q instead of\nthe corrected −Li_2^q(−z)).\n\nAxiomatised here pending a Lean infinite-product implementation;\nthe value at z = 0 is fixed by the empty-product convention. ","signatureChunk":0}]}